0..80 Comment "//! Access at a place. `access xs.#[i] as w { … }` lends one element of a held"
81..159 Comment "//! list to a view: the index is a value read where the access stands, and the"
160..239 Comment "//! view is the element at it. An exclusive view writes its element back at its"
240..320 Comment "//! index and the rest of the list stands as it was; a shared view reads it. The"
321..399 Comment "//! held list is lent as a whole, whatever the index, so two views of one list"
400..476 Comment "//! stand together only when both are shared. The place follows Rust\'s index"
477..542 Comment "//! expression on a place [Rust-reference], § Index expressions."
543..546 Comment "//!"
547..576 Comment "//! - cites: [Rust-reference]"
577..580 Comment "//!"
581..678 Comment "//! [Rust-reference]: https://doc.rust-lang.org/reference/ \"The Rust Project, The Rust Reference\""
